    "math_academy_id": "q-183823",
    "knowledge_point_id": "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff",
    "knowledge_point": "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval",
    "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.18<Z<0.18).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3594\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3974\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4364\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ |",
    "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.18<Z<0.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/061aec33cb30172ec64c89841fc70cb2e5bec9b89f92ef0427ff9673bfa99219.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =P(Z<0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =Φ(0.18)-Φ(-0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.18)=0.4286,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(0.18).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.18) & =P(Z\\le 0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =1-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.5714\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =Φ(0.18)-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =0.5714-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.1428.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
